#. Translators: What's new for this version, shown in the add-on store.
#. Markdown: NVDA renders it and reads it line by line.
#: manifest.ini:changelog
msgid ""
"- New, experimental: Petlibro feeders and water fountains (Air Smart Feeder PLAF108, Dockstream 2 Cordless PLWF116).\n"
"- New: platform status (Ctrl+P in the device menu).\n"
"- New: the heating times of the Cozytouch heat pump can be changed.\n"
"- NVDA+Ctrl+Shift+P announces a summary; pressed twice, it lists every device.\n"
"- The platforms sign in at the same time, and a sign-in that failed because of the network is retried automatically.\n"
"- A platform fault is announced only once it has lasted two minutes.\n"
"- The history records changes made elsewhere for all platforms, and what a device does on its own as automatic.\n"
"- Ctrl+F in the device menu now finds devices.\n"
"- NVDA no longer freezes while a VeSync, Netatmo or Meross lamp command is sent.\n"
"- Email addresses are stored encrypted, and removing the add-on deletes the stored credentials.\n"
"- Settings of an early version, including the Netatmo password in plain text, are removed from nvda.ini.\n"
"- NVDA starts faster, and Netatmo is polled with far fewer requests.\n"
"- Decimal numbers use the separator of the interface language.\n"
"- Network and server faults no longer play NVDA's error sound."
msgstr ""

